<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Maclodio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1427">1427</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-in-lombardy">Wars in Lombardy</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Maclodio was fought in October 1427 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> between the Venetian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-bussone-da-carmagnola">Francesco Bussone da Carmagnola</a> and the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti">Filippo Maria Visconti</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. Carmagnola, formerly Milan's leading captain, drew the Milanese into marshy ground and won a complete victory. The peace of 1428 confirmed Venetian possession of Brescia and added Bergamo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-maclodio.jpg" alt="Battle of Maclodio" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Lorenzo Gatteri and Francesco Zanotto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:70._Vittoria_dei_Veneziani_a_Maclodio_sopra_le_armi_del_Duca_di_Milano,_11_Ottobre_1427.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
